cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use QualiTranslate, please cite it as below and report the tools, models and review steps used (the methods record in each download lists them)."
title: "QualiTranslate: forward translation, blind back-translation, reconciliation and recorded human review for qualitative interview transcripts"
version: 1.5.1
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/AliYalcinkayaMD/qualitranslate"
url: "https://github.com/AliYalcinkayaMD/qualitranslate"
authors:
  - family-names: Yalcinkaya
    given-names: Ali
    affiliation: "Interdisciplinary Orthopaedics Research Group, Aalborg University Hospital, Denmark"
keywords:
  - qualitative research
  - translation
  - back-translation
  - cross-language research
  - large language models
abstract: >-
  QualiTranslate is a Python and R package for translating qualitative interview
  transcripts with large language models. It separates forward translation, blind
  back-translation and reconciliation, requires a recorded human decision for every
  section, and exports the prompts, replies, audit trail and a draft methods paragraph.
